        "id": 1139038
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-10T10:05:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`slice::len` is a method so you\u0027d use the dot notation, `self.len()`. There will be a naming clash as `len()` is already defined for `u8. That might not be a big deal if they are defined the same way but could be avoided.\n\nGiven `ReadOnlyDataByChunk::len` is only used to calculate the number of chunks and doesn\u0027t seem to be fit as part of the `ReadOnlyDataByChunk` trait (rather than type implementing this trait), would it be better to drop it from the trait in favour of just the method for length in chunks? You could impl `ReadOnlyDataByChunk` (`ReadDataByChunk` might be a better name as the implementing type might not be read-only and the trait doesn\u0027t actually mind about that) on `File` directly as well. File would have a slightly more expensive chunk counting method, but that\u0027s not often used.",
      "parentUuid": "d165fb83_d3f5ebdf",
      "revId": "b514af084df7131ecadfcb237c5fab252c6da4b0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
